# Development Rules

## Services and dependencies

- During development use free/open-source/self-hostable resources.
- Do not require new external accounts or paid services without explicit approval.
- Keep payment, identity verification, and messaging integrations replaceable until providers are approved.
- OSM public demo services are acceptable for development only; respect production usage policies.
- Do not fake provider credentials or claim external integrations are complete.

## Commands

Use Node 24 and pnpm 11. Prefer scoped commands because mobile is out of scope:

```bash
pnpm --filter @jrst/api start
pnpm --filter @jrst/web dev
pnpm --filter @jrst/api typecheck
pnpm --filter @jrst/web typecheck
pnpm --filter @jrst/api lint
pnpm --filter @jrst/web lint
pnpm --filter @jrst/api test
pnpm --filter @jrst/api build
pnpm --filter @jrst/web build
```

Root Turbo checks include mobile and should not be the only scoped verification.

## Verification and deployment

- Verify changes in proportion to risk, starting with focused checks.
- Inspect e2e scripts before use; several still target the retired Events journey.
- Do not deploy from the CLI. Use the repository's CI/CD path.
- Do not run Prisma migrations in application startup.
- Treat Render free-tier cold starts and earlier local Turbopack memory exhaustion as operational conditions, not application correctness.

